{{also|Jaffa}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{term|Jaffa}}, an ancient port city in Israel from where the oranges were exported.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A type of sweet orange, normally seedless.
# {{context|slang}} An impotent or infertile male.  The term comes from the "seedless" orange
#: "I've heard he's a jaffa."
# {{context|cricket}} A [[ball]] that is very [[difficult]] for the [[batsman]] to [[hit]] because it moves [[erratically]] either through the [[air]] or off the [[pitch]]
# {{context|NZ}} A type of confectionery consisting of a sphere of chocolate in a red casing.

